
================================================================
 CORTEX-M SECURITY POSTURE  (family: nrf-approtect)
================================================================
 (1) IDENTITY (FICR)
   INFO.PART              0x00052840 (e.g. 0x52840)
   INFO.VARIANT           0x00000000 (ASCII build code)
   RAM / FLASH            256 KB / 1024 KB
   DEVICEID               0000000000000000
 (2) READOUT PROTECTION (UICR.APPROTECT @0x10001208)
   APPROTECT              0x00000000 -> ENABLED is the configured intent — a reset re-locks; only re-open is a CTRL-AP mass-erase (WIPE)
 (3) DEBUG / OUTPUT
   DEBUGCTRL              0xffffffff (CPUNIDEN/CPUFPBEN; 0xFFFFFFFF = all debug allowed)
   REGOUT0 (VOUT)         0xffffffff
================================================================
 NOTE: reading any of the above proves the AHB-AP is OPEN -> internal flash is dumpable now.
================================================================
